# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Pinned set for the fine-tuning script (speech/train/README.md), separate from
# the conversion set of speech/convert/. GPU training on Linux x86_64 with an
# NVIDIA driver for CUDA 13.0 (R580 or newer; the CUDA 13 wheels of PyPI torch
# 2.13). Every version, transitive ones included, was published on or before
# 2026-10-22, like the conversion set (PyPI dates checked on 2026-11-05).
# Security update of 2026-11-05 (docs/dependencies.md): datasets 5.0.1, fsspec
# 2026.6.0, transformers 5.10.1 (5.10.0 was yanked) and torch 2.13.0 are the
# lowest fixed versions, accelerate 1.15.0 the latest. Pins that the new set no
# longer accepted moved to the newest version published before the cutoff that
# satisfies every requirement; the others are unchanged.
# Regenerate requirements.txt with its hashes, from the conversion venv:
#   speech/convert/.venv/Scripts/python speech/convert/lock.py hash --dir speech/train
#   speech/convert/.venv/Scripts/python speech/convert/lock.py check --dir speech/train
# lock-platforms: linux-x86_64
# lock-pythons: 3.11 3.12

